  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young Lives new phase, growth research contributions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This globally respected research programme provides high impact open access and gender disaggregated data on educational access and outcomes, skills and transition to labour markets. Data over 15 years allows us to follow the paths of 12,000 children from early years through adolescence and into early adulthood, gaining valuable insights on educational trajectories and access to higher education and labour market entry. This project covers the contributions from the Growth Research Team.</narrative>
  </description>
